+### CI failure triage (user report: red since PR #638)
+- Failing gate: `tests/regression/check_phi_acyclic_order` — "default rot()
+  does not beat gcc on size (56 vs 56 insns)".
+- Reproduced the oracle asymmetry: GH runners' GCC 13.3 compiles rot() to
+  55-56/0 (scalar shape); the local Debian GCC 14.2 goes SIMD on the prologue
+  (71/0), which is why the gate passed locally and failed only on CI.
+- lccc's side: the acyclic arm had drifted 55/3 → 56/3 — one relay mov per
+  iteration. The relay is structural: a computed φ incoming (`e = d + t1`)
+  is defined at the computation's original position, where all φ homes are
+  still occupied, so it must get its own home and be copied into the φ home.
+  Ordinary coalescing cannot remove it — at that point the values interfere.
+
+### Root fix (src/ir/mem2reg/phi_eliminate.rs)
+1. `plan_edge_copies_guards`: the acyclic Kahn scheduler now defers a ready
+   copy while some still-pending copy's computed source reads its
+   destination, so the clobbering copy (`d <- c`) is ordered after e's slot.
+   A full starved round falls back to plain Kahn (progress is guaranteed);
+   guard-free inputs produce the identical order (pinned by the existing
+   exhaustive enumerator + rotation tests).
+2. `fold_computed_phi_incomings` (acyclic policy only): sinks the pure ALU
+   definition (whitelist: Add/Sub/Mul/And/Or/Xor/Shl/AShr/LShr/BitTest/
+   Rotate — no div/rem (trap), no memory) to directly before its relay copy.
+   Hazard-checked: no reader of the relayed value and no writer of the
+   computation's operands strictly between (calls included via the
+   exhaustive `dest()` helper); a second def of the value in the window also
+   refuses. The parallel `source_spans` entry moves with the instruction.
+   The collapsed interval lets the existing RA copy coalescer union the pair;
+   the copy elides at emission. IR def structure untouched — the SSA
+   validator's post-elimination discipline (one Copy per edge) is preserved.
+- Red-team catch on myself: the first cut RENAMED the definition into the φ
+  value (BinOp+Copy double-def) — the validator rejected it on 485 corpus
+  files, exactly its job. Second cut (rename with downstream rewrite) was
+  dropped in favour of the def-discipline-preserving sink. A bookkeeping
+  index slip (removed a neighbouring rotation copy instead of the relay) was
+  caught by the new rotation fold unit test and is now pinned by a
+  debug_assert. Do not "simplify" the bottom-up candidate order: chained
+  computations (a = t1+t2 reading t1) need the farthest slot folded first.
+
+### Validation
+- Unit: 3612 pass / 0 fail (incl. 4 new φ-arity tests, planner deferral,
